gai5(){return"Where do I start? Depends on your case"},
gahQ(){return"Case A \u2014 I already have crops planted"},
gahG(){return"Crops: review Coffee and Plantain and set their stage to Producing (and, if you know it, area and live plants)."},
gahH(){return"Record: enter the month's expenses (supplies, labor)."},
gahI(){return"Record: when you sell, add an income with the kilos and the money you received; that crop's harvest is logged on its own from those kilos."},
gahJ(){return"Open Overview and check your numbers: harvested, cost per kilo and margin."},
gahK(){return"Check the Overview: balance and indicators start making sense."},
gai_(){return"I have nothing yet and I am starting"},
gahR(){return"Tell the app what you are going to plant: in Crops create your crop (coffee or plantain, for example) and set the stage to Not producing yet. Add the area if you know it."},
gahS(){return'In Plantings, record how many plants you put in and on what area, and the cost if you want. If your crop is not in the list, pick "Create new crop" and you create it right there.'},
gahT(){return"While the crop is not producing yet the app does not flag losses: it is investment, not production."},
gahU(){return"When it starts Producing, follow the Case A flow: the sales, and that is where your harvest comes from."},
gai4(){return"Renewing the whole plantation"},
gai0(){return"A full renewal is recorded as a new sowing of the same crop."},
gai1(){return"That resets age, plants and area; old harvests stay in the history."},
gai2(){return"If crops share the same plot (coffee with plantain, for example), the clearest way is to create a separate crop for each."},
gai3(){return"Nothing needs to be deleted: the history still counts what already happened."},
gajZ(){return"Units"},
gajL(){return"Use kg, pounds (lb), arroba (12.5 kg), sacks or load (27.2 kg). The app converts everything to kg for comparison, using the sack weight you set in Settings."},
gajY(){return"Equivalences"},
