gaj1(){return"Margin per ha"},
gaiY(){return"Sales \u2212 expenses, per hectare. Positive = the hectare leaves profit."},
gaj4(){return"Why normalize? A 3 ha plot selling COP 9,000,000 does not compete with a 1 ha plot selling COP 5,000,000: per hectare, the second one wins. The panel divides by area so you compare by the same rule."},
gaiR(){return"How is the establishment investment recovered?"},
gaiO(){return"When editing a crop you can record the Total investment: what you invested in planting and raising the crop (seedlings, labor, initial fertilization\u2026)."},
gaiT(){return"% recovered"},
gaiQ(){return"The app divides the crop's accumulated margin (sales \u2212 expenses) by that investment. 100% = you have paid it off."},
gaiU(){return"Payback in N years (approx.)"},
gaiV(){return"Average of the measured annual margin. It is an average of your real data, not a harvest promise."},
gaiS(){return"It is not a loss: it is an investment"},
gaiP(){return"If you invest COP 1,000,000 planting coffee and have not sold yet, you did not lose COP 1,000,000. You invested COP 1,000,000. When you start selling, the recovery percentage starts to rise."},
gaiE(){return"The order of the app"},
